    "note": "Version read: Amended 2019-06-20 (Senate 2019-09-09 and final Assembly 2019-09-10 votes on it; Assembly's earlier votes were on the 2019-05-24 text). Marked changes in this version: Section 28225 fee struck 'fourteen dollars ($14)' -> 'one dollar ($1)'; Section 28233 fee struck 'thirteen dollars and nineteen cents ($13.19)' -> '$31.19' and the deposit account renamed Dealers' Record of Sale Supplemental Subaccount. The gun-show sections (27205-27345) print without marks in this version (amended in earlier versions)."
  },
  "operative_text": "Section 27205 (Penal Code): (a) Before commencement of a gun show or event, the producer thereof shall, upon written request from a law enforcement agency with jurisdiction over the facility, make available to that agency, within 48 hours or a later time specified by the agency, a complete and accurate list of all persons, entities, and organizations that have leased or rented, or are known to the producer to intend to lease or rent, any table, display space, or area at the gun show or event for the purpose of selling, leasing, or transferring firearms, or processing the sale or transfer of ammunition.\nSection 27235 (Penal Code): Every producer of a gun show or event shall have a written contract with each gun show vendor selling firearms or ammunition at the show or event.\nSection 27310 (Penal Code): All firearms and ammunition transfers or sales at a gun show or event shall be in accordance with applicable state and federal laws.\nSection 27345 (Penal Code): Any person who possesses a firearm or ammunition at a gun show or event shall have government-issued photo identification in immediate possession, and shall display it upon request to any security officer or peace officer.\nSection 28225 (Penal Code): (a) The Department of Justice may require the dealer to charge each firearm purchaser a fee not to exceed one dollar ($1), except that the fee may be increased at a rate not to exceed any increase in the California Consumer Price Index as compiled and reported by the Department of Industrial Relations.\nSection 28233 (Penal Code): (a) The Department of Justice may, in addition to the fee described in Sections 28225 and 28230, require a dealer to charge each firearm purchaser a fee in the amount of thirty-one dollars and nineteen cents ($31.19)."
}